  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Total surface area of a cube is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Volume of a cube&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p>Change in volume is given by,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>&#947;</mi><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>T</mi></math>,&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mn>8</mn></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mn>10</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p>",
